tent": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Writes simple but clear texts describing or reviewing places to visit in the region, using an appropriate range of vocabulary and grammatical structures."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Writes simple but clear texts describing or reviewing places to visit in the region, using an appropriate range of vocabulary and grammatical structures."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Writes simple but clear texts describing or reviewing places to visit in the region, using an appropriate range of vocabulary and grammatical structures."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About Banking"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The people you talk to at the bank are called <span class=\"strong\">bank tellers</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "They can help you with many things like: <li>opening an account <li>depositing money into your bank account <li>taking out money out of your account<li>cashing checks<li>applying for a credit card</li>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you are at the bank, the bank teller can make <span class=\"italic\">offers</span>. You can <span class=\"italic\">accept</span> or <span class=\"italic\">reject </span> these offers. It is important to be polite by saying thanks and saying no politely.  <br/> At the bank, it is common for you to make requests. You can use <span class=\"italic\">modals</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Infinitives</span> to make requests."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Bank Teller</span>: How may I help you? <br><span class=\"strong\">Customer</span>: I would like to open an account.<br>   <span class=\"strong\">Bank Teller</span>: Would you like to apply for a credit card also?   <br><span class=\"strong\">Customer</span>: No, thanks."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Possessive Adjectives and Pronouns"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Possessive pronouns can take the place of nouns. You use possessive pronouns to talk about things that belong to someone. <br> You use possessive adjectives to describe nouns. They come before the noun."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Possessive  Adjectives\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Possessive Pronouns\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">my</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">mine</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">your</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">yours</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">his</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">his</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" She\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">her</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">hers</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">our</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">ours</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" They\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">their</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">theirs</span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "convenient"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "useful to you because it saves time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is convenient for travel, right?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob11aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are the words to review."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to upgrade"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give someone a better seat on a plane  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Would you like to upgrade to first class?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob11aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "checking account"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a bank account that you can take money out of at any time, and can use checks to pay for things "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I would like to deposit it into my checking account."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob11aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to deposit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put money in a bank"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I would like to deposit money into my account. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob11aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to withdraw "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to remove money from the bank"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can withdraw money during the day."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob11aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to transfer"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to move money from one account into another"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'd like to transfer $100 into my savings account."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob11aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "funds"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an amount of available money"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can add more when you run low on funds."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob11aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fee"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an amount paid of for a service "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The credit card has a yearly fee."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob11aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "promotion"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an activity to help sell a product"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  We have a promotion going on right now."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob11aud09"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn3le05ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Visit the website of the largest bank in your city. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Research their checking or saving accounts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Visit another bank's website."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 3 sentences about the information you find."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your information with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write about banking and money."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I express possession."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write complete statements about banking information."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about banking with a partner."}]}], "type": "sena"}